  "details": "Description:\n\nWhen creating a world instance, the instance name can be set up to 50 characters, but the in-game UI only displays up to the first 18 full-width characters (e.g., Japanese). Anything beyond that is cut off, and there is currently no way to view the full instance name inside the game.\n\nOn the VRChat website, longer instance names are visible to some extent, so being completely unable to read the full name in-game appears to be a UI bug. Please look into this issue.\n\nSteps to Reproduce:\n\nOpen the instance creation menu in-game.\n\nEnter an instance name longer than 18 full-width characters (up to the 50-character limit).\n\nCreate the instance and check the instance name in the in-game UI (such as the Launch Pad / World details).\n\nExpected Result:\n\nThe full instance name (up to 50 characters) should be readable in-game (e.g., via text wrapping, scrolling, or a tooltip).\n\nActual Result:\n\nOnly the first 18 full-width characters are displayed, and the rest cannot be viewed anywhere in-game.",
